test_ip_reasm2 — IPv4 reassembly RFC corners
=============================================

Two test-only IPC drivers in inet validate the new RFC corners
on top of the basic reassembly path:

- **RFC 5722 overlap drop.** Inject a first-fragment ('X'x16)
  followed by a fragment that overlaps it ('Y'x8 at offset=8).
  The slot must be poisoned and never assemble.
- **ICMP Time Exceeded on timeout.** Inject one first-fragment,
  force-expire its deadline, run the scan sweep. The server
  bumps `inet_ip_reasm_timeouts_sent` whether or not the wire
  send actually succeeds, so the test verifies the emit attempt.

Prints `test_ip_reasm2: ok` on pass or `test_ip_reasm2: failed N`
where N is the failing sub-test number.

    module oskit.bin.test_ip_reasm2

    import oskit.ulib.{puts, exit, exit_with}
    import oskit.net.{ip_reasm_overlap_test, ip_reasm_timeout_test}


    print_udec(v: int)
        if v >= 10
            print_udec(v / 10)
        var b: [1]byte
        b[0] = byte('0' + (v % 10))
        puts(string(&b[0], 1))


    fail(code: int)
        puts("test_ip_reasm2: failed ")
        print_udec(code)
        puts("\n")
        exit_with(code)


    main(argv: []string)
        val r1 = ip_reasm_overlap_test()
        if r1 != 0
            fail(10 + r1)
            return

        val r2 = ip_reasm_timeout_test()
        if r2 != 0
            fail(20 + r2)
            return

        puts("test_ip_reasm2: ok\n")
        exit()
